-group-type="author"><name><surname>McRobert</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Tompkins</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The effect of <italic>transformer, doublesex</italic> and <italic>intersex</italic> mutations on the sexual behavior of <italic>Drosophila melanogaster</italic></article-title><source>Genetics</source><year>1985</year><volume>111</volume><fpage>89</fpage><lpage>96</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3928434</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Villella</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ryner</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Baker</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Behavioral and neurobiological implications of sex-determining factors in <italic>Drosophila</italic></article-title><source>Dev. Genet</source><year>1994</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>275</fpage><lpage>296</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8062459</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Villella</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Courtship anomalies caused by <italic>doublesex</italic> mutations in <italic>Drosophila melanogaster</italic></article-title><source>Genetics</source><year>1996</year><volume>143</volume><fpage>331</fpage><lpage>344</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8722785</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gailey</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Behavior and cytogenetics of <italic>fruitless</italic> in <italic>Drosophila melanogaster</italic>: different courtship defects caused by separate, closely linked lesions</article-title><source>Genetics</source><year>1989</year><volume>121</volume><fpage>773</fpage><lpage>785</lpage><comment>[published erratum appears in <italic>Genetics</italic> 1989,122:465]</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2542123</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goodwin</surname><given-names>SF</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Villella</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Foss</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ryner</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Baker</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Aberrant splicing and altered spatial expression patterns in <italic>fruitless</italic> mutants of <italic>Drosophila melanogaster</italic></article-title><source>Genetics</source><year>2000</year><volume>154</volume><fpage>725</fpage><lpage>745</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10655225</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ito</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Fujitani</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Usui</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Shimizu-Nishikawa</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanaka</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamamoto</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sexual orientation in <italic>Drosophila</italic> is altered by the <italic>satori</italic> mutation in the sex-determination gene <italic>fruitless</italic> that encodes a zinc finger protein with a BTB domain</article-title><source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. U.S.A</source><year>1996</year><volume>93</volume><fpage>9687</fpage><lpage>9692</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8790392</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ryner</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodwin</surname><given-names>SF</given-names></name><name><surname>Castrillon</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name><name><surname>Anand</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Villella</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Baker</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wasserman</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Control of male sexual behavior and sexual orientation in <italic>Drosophila</italic> by the <italic>fruitless</italic> gene</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>1996</year><volume>87</volume><fpage>1079</fpage><lpage>1089</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8978612</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Villella</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gailey</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Berwald</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohshima</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Barnes</surname><given-names>PT</given-names></name><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Extended reproductive roles of the <italic>fruitless</italic> gene in <italic>Drosophila melanogaster</italic> revealed by behavioral analysis of new <italic>fru</italic> mutants</article-title><source>Genetics</source><year>1997</year><volume>147</volume><fpage>1107</fpage><lpage>1130</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9383056</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Baker</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Are complex behaviors specified by dedicated regulatory genes? Reasoning from <italic>Drosophila</italic></article-title><source>Cell</source><year>2001</year><volume>105</volume><fpage>13</fpage><lpage>24</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11300999</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R16"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Billeter</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Rideout</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Dornan</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodwin</surname><given-names>SF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Control of male sexual behavior in <italic>Drosophila</italic> by the sex determination pathway</article-title><source>Curr. Biol</source><year>2006</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>R766</fpage><lpage>776</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16950103</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R17"><label>17</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Manoli</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Meissner</surname><given-names>